  nonce: 70ad  # 70ad
  message: "DONE in PR (dev 6f8da9d036). Fixed the titled py.py mislabel: the unresolved method-call fallback stamped resolution_quality='type_inferred' UNCONDITIONALLY, including on the give-up branch whose own comment reads 'type cannot be inferred'. Now DERIVED from whether the receiver-hint chain actually established a type — self (enclosing_class) / annotated-or-constructed var / bare local class keep 'type_inferred'; the untyped/duck give-up (INV-fahub-biased to unresolved) carries NO resolution_quality (the field names the resolution pathway per spec §903, and here there was none).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the filing's own repro on the current corpus, analyze_python on /tmp/f5_cohort_pool/pretix/src): give-up mislabels 7920 -> 0; every remaining type_inferred (7692) carries a real inference signal (receiver_type_hint / enclosing_class / receiver_type_id, or a module-qualified typed dst). NOTE the filing's '0/16301 actually type-inferred' is now STALE — the WI-noham/WI-supat/WI-fuvuj/WI-sozoj receiver-hint work made ~38% legitimately typed before this fix; this fix removes the false label from the remaining ~62% give-ups. Unit test test_py_resolution_quality.py::test_give_up_receiver_carries_no_resolution_quality pins the give-up branch directly; 574 receiver-resolution/coherence regression tests pass, changed source 100% in isolation.\n\nThe 3 genuinely-type-inferred py.py stamps (WI-fuvuj external_var_types, WI-noham property-read line 4037, WI-sozoj django marker) were already correct and are unchanged.\n\nSEPARATE (not this item's titled defect, flagged for owner): the discussion also noted cross-ANALYZER resolution_quality vocabulary inconsistency (py/dart/csharp 'type_inferred', lua 'typed', ruby 'typed_receiver', go 'ambiguous') + whether csharp/dart have the SAME give-up mislabel. That's a vocabulary-normalization + per-analyzer audit, distinct from the Python fix. Not filed — surfaced to owner."  # 70ad
